  beschreibung: Mercury is the smallest planet and orbits closest to the Sun. Its
    surface is full of impact craters and looks similar to the Moon because Mercury
    has almost no atmosphere to slow meteoroids or store heat. Temperatures therefore
    change extremely between hot days and very cold nights. One Mercury year lasts
    only about 88 Earth days.
  planetSizeInfoText: Mercury is the smallest planet. Its diameter is only about
    38 percent of Earth's diameter.
  orbitalDistanceInfoText: At 0.39 AU, Mercury is the planet closest to the Sun and
    receives very intense solar energy.
  orbitalSpeedInfoText: Mercury moves very quickly on its tight orbit. One orbit
    takes only about 88 Earth days.
  axialTiltInfoText: Mercury's axis is almost not tilted at all, so it has hardly
    any classical seasons.
  eccentricityInfoText: Mercury's orbit is much more oval than the orbits of most
    planets. Its distance from the Sun changes strongly.
  planetScaleInfoText: In a size comparison, Mercury is smaller than all other planets
    and only a little larger than the Moon.
  gravityInfoText: Gravity is about 38 percent of Earth's gravity. A 10 kg object
    would feel like about 3.8 kg there.
  fakten:
  - Mercury's surface is covered with impact craters and looks similar to Earth's
    Moon.
  - Mercury has almost no atmosphere, so temperatures change extremely between day
    and night.
  - Water ice may survive inside permanently shadowed craters near Mercury's poles.
